Z||000000||mrgone||05-12-2001||02:34 PM||||ok in a little bit im going to take apart my dash to try and solve some problems,<BR>ive never done anything like this before<P>my problems are, my interior fan isnt blowing anything even when on hi but the rad fan ajusts when i turn the switch up.<P>my oil and coolent guages arent working properly<P>the guage lights are too dim... <P>im going to check the fuses first. <BR>will take a pic of the fusebox with my camera in case i dont remember where i pulled it from||||reg||11
Z||000001||Nashco||05-12-2001||03:20 PM||||There are a few things you should check before tearing into your dash.<P>Firstly, have you checked to make sure the rheostat is working for the dash lights.  When you adjust the light intensity, does it change?  If not, you just need a new rheostat, if so, you probably have some bulbs burnt out.<P>Secondly, have you checked the sending units for the guages?  Perhaps you just need new sending units.  It's a lot easier to replace a sending unit than a guage, in some circumstances.<P>Your interior fan statement boggles me...the radiator fan shouldn't "adjust" when you turn the fan up, unless you are turning the AC controls on.  If you have the AC on, the fan should come on automatically.<P>Good luck, sounds like you have some work ahead of you.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
